# SilverBullet stack secrets (services VM)
# Copy to .sops.env and encrypt with:
#   sops -e -i .sops.env
#
# Key-set contract: this file, the real .sops.env and the test fixture
# tests/fixtures/silverbullet.sops.env must all carry EXACTLY the same keys —
# the stack-env-drift lint fails on any difference.
#
# ⚠ Both services in the stack read this one file (compose gives every service
# the same env_file), so SilverBullet also sees GIT_SYNC_REMOTE and the sync
# sidecar also sees SB_USER. Neither is used by the other; keep it in mind
# before adding a key whose NAME would mean something to SilverBullet.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SB_USER — SilverBullet's own login, as `username:password`.
#
# This is the SECOND lock. Caddy's `import protected` (Authentik forward auth)
# is the first, and SilverBullet cannot read the X-Authentik-* headers, so
# this is two logins permanently — the Windmill posture. It stays because the
# service is loopback-published: if a route is ever flipped or the outpost is
# down, this is what keeps the space closed.
#
# 🚨 If the password contains '$', SINGLE-QUOTE the whole value (finding #30):
# decrypt-sops-envs writes a plain .env that is later sourced, and an
# unquoted '$' is expanded away silently.
#
# Lockout is built in: 10 failed attempts, 60s lockout (SB_LOCKOUT_LIMIT /
# SB_LOCKOUT_TIME, both left at their defaults).
# Generate: openssl rand -base64 24
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SB_USER=idan:changeme_openssl_rand_base64_24

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GIT_SYNC_REMOTE — the Forgejo repository the space is mirrored to, WITH
# credentials in the URL.
#
# Shape:  http://<forgejo-user>:<PAT>@127.0.0.1:10550/<owner>/<repo>.git
#
#   - http, not https, and 127.0.0.1:10550, not forgejo.svc.idanreed.com: the
#     sync sidecar is host-networked and talks to Forgejo's loopback publish
#     directly. The PAT never leaves the host, nothing depends on DNS, the
#     wildcard certificate, Caddy or the tailnet, and Forgejo being briefly
#     down is a retry rather than a failure.
#   - Forgejo has SSH DISABLED (stacks/forgejo/compose.yaml sets
#     FORGEJO__server__DISABLE_SSH=true), so a deploy key is not an option and
#     a PAT is the only credential that works.
#
# Operator steps, none of which are done for you:
#   1. Create the repository in Forgejo (private). This stack does NOT create
#      it — a sync script that can create repositories is a sync script that
#      can create the WRONG repository.
#   2. Settings -> Applications -> Generate Token, scopes: `write:repository`
#      only. Nothing else is needed and anything else is blast radius.
#   3. Put the token here. If it contains '$', single-quote the value.
#
# Until this is real, git-sync.sh detects the `changeme` substring and alerts
# through ntfy once an hour rather than pretending to mirror (the same gate
# stacks/backrest/config-init.sh applies to DEADMAN_URL). SilverBullet itself
# works fine meanwhile — only the mirror is off.
#
# ⚠ The Obsidian side is the OTHER writer, and the conflict rule is
# REMOTE-WINS: on a page edited in both places the Obsidian version survives
# and the SilverBullet version is kept on a local rescue branch. Read the
# header of git-sync.sh before relying on it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GIT_SYNC_REMOTE=http://changeme_forgejo_user:changeme_forgejo_pat@127.0.0.1:10550/changeme_owner/changeme_repo.git
